<title>SINGAPORE: Heshe gets new substantial shareholder.</title>
<headline>Heshe gets new substantial shareholder.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retailer Heshe Holdings said on Monday that Ho Hoi Han has bought 30 million shares -- a 9.62 percent stake -- at Singapore $0.45 each in the retial firm.</p>
<p>The shares were bought from Tan Sim Chew, who declared last week he had agreed to sell a 19 percent stake, or 59.2 million shares, in Heshe.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
